# shell: both
# Stage 2, on the fact stage 4 needed first: the window CHANGES and the
# reader is told.  The conducted driver subscribes on its first
# expect-told and after that only listens -- the shell speaks first.
# The in-process driver composes the same bounded claim by asking each
# turn; the same file proves it twice, two ways.
#
# The change is the spec's own example: a copy runs to its finish, and
# there is no wait line between the paste and the claim -- waiting on
# "the copy finished" without a wait-loop is exactly what this stage
# exists to remove.
wait 12
expect-told a.txt
note the watch stands; a copy now runs to its finish
key a ctrl
wait 3
key c ctrl
wait 3
key v ctrl
expect-told a.txt copy
quit
